.el .ds Aq '
.TH focusforge-cli-sharp-areas 1  "sharp-areas 0.2.1" 
.SH NAME
focusforge\-cli\-sharp\-areas \- Count the areas of the image that are sharpest in each frame of a stack
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfocusforge\-cli sharp\-areas\fR [\fB\-\-set\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-priority\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDIR\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Count the areas of the image that are sharpest in each frame of a stack.
.PP
The image is divided into square cells. A cell is counted in the frame where its mean focus score peaks, when that peak exceeds the contrast times the cell\*(Aqs lowest score over the stack; a cell without that contrast is counted in no frame. Frames are counted as read, without alignment.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fI<KEY=VALUE>\fR
Set a parameter: `\-\-set key=value`, repeatable. A repeated key is last\-wins
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the counts as one JSON object
.TP
\fB\-\-priority\fR \fI<PRIORITY>\fR [default: normal]
How many frames are read at once; the counts are the same at either value
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
low: One frame at a time, leaving the other cores to other work
.IP \(bu 2
normal: As many frames at once as the host has threads
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log detail (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Log errors only
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIDIR\fR>
Directory of frames to count (non\-recursive, descending into a `frames` subdirectory)
.SH EXTRA
Parameters (\-\-set KEY=VALUE):
  cell\-size      Area size (px) (default 64, 16 to 512)
  contrast       Peak\-to\-floor contrast (default 2, 1 to 10)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.1
